
Frequent Unix Patching on Pre‑Production: With the shift to twice‑monthly Unix patches for both dev and ESQM regions, I orchestrated the end‑to‑end process—coordinating server reboots, verifying Finacle service restarts, and conducting smoke tests post‑patch. I developed a checklist‑based playbook that reduced patching time by 25% while ensuring no step was missed.

Technology Stack Upgrades: I sequentially drove multiple concurrent upgrades, each critical for security and supportability:

Apache JBCS connector upgrade to the latest supported version.

Autosys JRE update to patch critical vulnerabilities.

OpenJDK 8 minor version bump for the remaining JDK 8 instances.

Oracle client upgrade to 19c to stay aligned with the database tier.

Time machine (Delphix) software upgrade, ensuring data masking continued to function.

Filebeat upgrade to maintain log‑shipping to the central observability platform.

COF root‑certificate import into all pre‑production trust stores to prevent SSL handshake failures.

I performed these upgrades during maintenance windows, creating rollback plans for each, and validated them through a rigorous regression test suite.

Certificate and Account Lifecycle: I managed the renewal and rotation of 40+ internal certificates and 60+ database/service accounts across all environments, avoiding a single expiration that could have caused a service outage. I automated the password‑reset process using Ansible vault, which now securely updates and distributes credentials without human exposure.

Deposits Migration Support: The high‑profile deposits pilot migration demanded rigorous pre‑production dry runs and end‑to‑end cycles. I provided platform support for over 10 dress‑rehearsal runs, diagnosing connectivity and data‑synchronization issues, and tuning JVM heap settings to handle the migration load. My proactive monitoring caught a connection‑pool exhaustion during a parallel run, which we resolved before the production pilot, contributing to a flawless go‑live.

Alert Hygiene and Incident Response: I continuously reviewed and fine‑tuned over 200 production monitors, muting non‑critical alerts for test environments, adjusting thresholds to reduce false positives, and creating clear, actionable email templates. This not only reduced alert fatigue but also sharpened our mean‑time‑to‑respond for actual incidents.

